######## 62. Production: the agent marks what is named so, the human decides the rest

-- api's prod was drafted from a workflow and marked in A; here is one added by hand, read with the production account's profile

$ kagebunshin project add-env api production
warning: environment production of project api looks like production (its name has the segment production) and waits for a human decision; mark it sensitive with `kagebunshin mark env api production`, since it is production by its name, or ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`) and either mark api/production sensitive or acknowledge it is not production
added environment production to project api

$ kagebunshin project add-source api production --provider aws_sm --secret acme/prod/api --profile acme-prod
added a source to environment production of project api; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin --env production run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: environment production of project api looks like production (its name has the segment production) and waits for a human decision
hint: it is production by its name: mark it sensitive with `kagebunshin mark env api production`; its values are then handed out once the human approves the request in the app
[exit 5]

$ kagebunshin --json --env production run -- ./test.sh
{"code":"sensitive_env","message":"environment production of project api looks like production (its name has the segment production) and waits for a human decision","hint":"it is production by its name: mark it sensitive with `kagebunshin mark env api production`; its values are then handed out once the human approves the request in the app","who":"agent","tell":null}
[exit 5]

$ kagebunshin --env production status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  aws_sm  profile acme-prod  ok
project: api
env: production
2 keys
  API_KEY  aws_sm:acme/prod/api  sensitive
  API_URL  aws_sm:acme/prod/api  sensitive
missing (in .env.example, set by no source):
  DATABASE_URL
  SIGNING_KEY
  LOG_LEVEL
shared with other environments (marking production sensitive leaves these unmarked unless noted; a human can mark them as well in the app):
  aws_sm:acme/prod/api  also read by api.prod  sensitive: each of them needs approval for its keys
to fill in what is missing:
  you can run:
    kagebunshin project set-var api production LOG_LEVEL info
      (only if .env.example's value is the real setting, not a placeholder; a secret belongs in the store or a provider)
warning: environment production of project api looks like production (its name has the segment production) and waits for a human decision; mark it sensitive with `kagebunshin mark env api production`, since it is production by its name, or ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`) and either mark api/production sensitive or acknowledge it is not production

$ kagebunshin --env production next
project api, environment production: 2 of 5 keys set, and it is production by its name: mark it sensitive
next (you): mark api.production sensitive: it is production by its name, so its values are handed out only once the human approves the request in the app
  kagebunshin mark env api production

$ kagebunshin next
project api, environment dev: 5 of 5 keys set, proven; an environment named production is left to mark
next (you): mark api.production sensitive: it is production by its name, so its values are handed out only once the human approves the request in the app
  kagebunshin mark env api production

-- the agent marks it: no passphrase, no human

$ kagebunshin mark env api production
marked sensitive

$ kagebunshin --env production next
refusing environment production of project api: it is marked sensitive, so an agent is not shown what it holds and nothing here is yours to set up; `kagebunshin --env production run -- COMMAND` gets its values once the human approves it in the app

$ kagebunshin next
project api, environment dev: done. 5 of 5 keys set; `./test.sh` ran with them on <day>. They come from aws_sm:acme/dev/api (2), aws_sm:acme/dev/db (1), aws_sm:acme/dev/signing (1), the project file (1).

-- there is no command that takes a mark off or says it is not production

$ kagebunshin unmark env api production
error: unrecognized subcommand 'unmark'

  tip: a similar subcommand exists: 'mark'

Usage: kagebunshin [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

For more information, try '--help'.
[exit 2]

$ kagebunshin mark --help | grep -E '^  [a-z]'
  env     Mark an environment, and the secrets only its sources read
  secret  Mark one secret, wherever it is read
  key     Mark one key of the local store
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

-- the store takes the passphrase to write: the mark waits beside it until the next unlock

$ ls $HOME/.config/kagebunshin | grep store
store.age
store.age.lock
store.age.marks

$ kagebunshin lock
locked

(human) $ kagebunshin unlock
Passphrase for the local store: 
unlocked

$ ls $HOME/.config/kagebunshin | grep store
store.age
store.age.lock

$ kagebunshin --env prod run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: refusing environment prod of project api: it is marked sensitive; handing it out takes approval in the app, which is not open
hint: once the app is open, run the command again; the app asks to approve it
ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`), so a request for values marked sensitive can be approved there
[exit 5]

-- what only may be production is the human's to decide: an environment named rc

$ kagebunshin project add-env api rc
warning: environment rc of project api looks like production (its name has the segment rc) and waits for a human decision; ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`) and either mark api/rc sensitive or acknowledge it is not production
added environment rc to project api

$ kagebunshin --env rc next
project api, environment rc: 0 of 5 keys set, and it waits for the human's decision in the app
waiting on the human; tell them:
  - Please run `kagebunshin store set api.rc API_KEY API_URL DATABASE_URL SIGNING_KEY` in a terminal; it asks for the store passphrase, then each value.
  - Please open the kagebunshin app and decide about api.rc, which looks like production (its name has the segment rc): mark it sensitive, or acknowledge it is not production. Until then a run with it is refused, or asks you in the app.
nothing more you can do until the human has done the above

$ kagebunshin project add-env shop prod
warning: environment prod of project shop looks like production (its name has the segment prod) and waits for a human decision; mark it sensitive with `kagebunshin mark env shop prod`, since it is production by its name, or ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`) and either mark shop/prod sensitive or acknowledge it is not production
added environment prod to project shop

-- the human, in the app: api/rc -> Mark sensitive

-- both are marked sensitive, and the app is closed: refused at once

$ kagebunshin --env prod run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: refusing environment prod of project api: it is marked sensitive; handing it out takes approval in the app, which is not open
hint: once the app is open, run the command again; the app asks to approve it
ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`), so a request for values marked sensitive can be approved there
[exit 5]

$ kagebunshin --env prod next
refusing environment prod of project api: it is marked sensitive, so an agent is not shown what it holds and nothing here is yours to set up; `kagebunshin --env prod run -- COMMAND` gets its values once the human approves it in the app

-- the app is open: the run waits and the app asks. The human closes the app with no answer, and the run is refused

$ kagebunshin --env prod run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: refusing environment prod of project api: it is marked sensitive; handing it out takes approval in the app, which is not open
hint: once the app is open, run the command again; the app asks to approve it
ask the human: open the app (`kagebunshin app`), so a request for values marked sensitive can be approved there
[exit 5]

-- the app is open and the human does not answer: the run is refused once `approval_timeout` in config.toml is over (3 seconds here, 5 minutes unless set), and says what it asked for

$ kagebunshin --env prod run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: environment prod of project api: nobody answered the request within 3 seconds, so nothing was handed out. It asked for every value of the environment, which is marked sensitive
hint: run the command again once the human is at the screen: the app's window shows this command and takes the store's passphrase
ask the human: approve the request in the app (`kagebunshin app`) when it asks
[exit 5]

-- the human clicks Deny

$ kagebunshin --env prod run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: environment prod of project api: a person denied the request, so nothing was handed out. It asked for every value of the environment, which is marked sensitive
hint: a person refused this: ask them before running it again
[exit 5]

-- the human types the passphrase and clicks Approve

$ kagebunshin --env prod run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: warning: 2 keys in .env.example are not set by any source: SIGNING_KEY, LOG_LEVEL
ok   API_KEY
ok   API_URL
ok   DATABASE_URL
MISSING SIGNING_KEY
MISSING LOG_LEVEL
[exit 1]

-- the human, in the app: shop/prod -> Not production

$ kagebunshin --env prod status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  file  local store  ok
project: shop
env: prod
0 keys
missing (in .env.example, set by no source):
  DATABASE_URL
  STRIPE_SECRET
  PORT
to fill in what is missing:
  you can run:
    kagebunshin project set-var shop prod PORT 3000
      (only if .env.example's value is the real setting, not a placeholder; a secret belongs in the store or a provider)
  ask the human:
    kagebunshin store set shop.prod DATABASE_URL STRIPE_SECRET
      (it asks for the store passphrase, then each value)

$ kagebunshin --env prod run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: warning: 3 keys in .env.example are not set by any source: DATABASE_URL, STRIPE_SECRET, PORT
MISSING DATABASE_URL
MISSING STRIPE_SECRET
MISSING PORT
[exit 1]

-- what the human decided, an agent's mark does not undo

$ kagebunshin mark env shop prod
kagebunshin: environment prod of project shop is acknowledged as not production; a human decided that, and only they change it, in the app
[exit 5]
